    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (78.62) leading the charge. His matchup against Mitch Keller offers a pristine environment for production, bolstered by a strong platoon edge and a favorable slot in the three-hole, making him the premier play for speed and power. Right behind him, **James Wood** (76.28) is a must-start at leadoff against a vulnerable arm in Simeon Woods Richardson. **Wood**\u2019s elite xwOBA and the added cushion of a +10% order bonus position him as our most efficient source of volume. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) also earns a high-confidence start, capitalizing on a significant +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, rounding out an outfield trio that anchors our daily efficiency targets.\n\nAt the corners, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) is our strongest infield play, benefiting from a high-floor matchup against Cecconi and a beneficial wind forecast. The most difficult decision today centered on **Travis Bazzana** (56.70) and **Kyle Karros** (54.02); while both sit in the \"marginal\" tier, they narrowly edged out our deeper bench depth. **Trevor Story** (52.39) remains a high-risk, high-reward play despite the stiff competition from Griffin Jax, as his stolen base potential forces him into the lineup despite a sub-standard xERA matchup. We are strictly managing our game caps today, which keeps players like **Jose Caballero**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki** on the bench due to scheduled days off or lack of confirmed lineup spots, prioritizing the active efficiency of **Luis Campusano** and **Tyler Soderstrom**\u2014though both require monitoring, as \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Campusano** and **Soderstrom** introduces variability to their projected order bonuses.",
